title: noodle_context
---
// The Noodle dimension round the Noodly Temple (gate address ALDENTE): the
// village of Brothlehem, the Pilgrims' Way up to the temple, and Mount
// Fizzuvius, the soda volcano. One node per resident, named
// `noodle_<place>_<resident>`. The rooms are written by
// `game/ambition_map_assets/ambition_content/generators/noodle_village/make_specs.py`.
// Ramen-nujan, in the temple's narthex, is in `kernel.yarn`.
//
// Never played. No placement names this node; it declares the zone.
===

title: noodle_village_duckling
---
Duckling: Ah. A new arrival. Stand still, I am counting you.
-> What are you counting?
    Duckling: Pilgrims. Two hundred came through the ring this week. Each one copied the pilgrim before him: the colander hat, the bow, the word "Ramen" at the end of every sentence.
    Duckling: Nobody taught them. They caught it. That is what a meme is. I named the thing, you know.
-> Do you believe in Him?
    Duckling: I believe that people believe in Him. It is the most successful replicator I have ever seen, and it is made of pasta.
    Duckling: I came to study it. Three weeks later I own a colander. Draw your own conclusions.
-> Where do the roads go?
    Duckling: West is the Pilgrims' Way: through the wheat, up the stair, to the temple's door. Everyone goes west.
    Duckling: East is the market, then the springs, then Mount Fizzuvius. Nobody goes east twice. The soda stings.
-> Carry on.
===

title: noodle_village_curry
---
Marie Curry: Sit. The udon is ready. The curry is nearly ready. Do not touch the pot that glows.
-> What is the soda on the mountain?
    Marie Curry: Carbonic acid: water with carbon dioxide forced into it. The mountain makes the gas, and the springs carry it up.
    Marie Curry: It is a weak acid. Weak is not the same as nothing. It will sting you and throw you out, and you will not float in it.
-> Why does it erupt?
    Marie Curry: A nucleation event. The gas waits for a rough surface to form bubbles on. A mint is very rough, at a small scale.
    Marie Curry: A thousand years ago someone dropped a mint in the vent. Someone else took it out. The mountain has been calm since. I have checked.
-> Why curry, in a temple town?
    Marie Curry: The pilgrims eat noodles three times a day. I add a variable. Precision matters in both science and cooking.
-> Thank you.
===

title: noodle_fizzy_hermit
---
Weird Hermit: Stop. Do you have mints?
-> No mints.
    Weird Hermit: Good. Good. The mountain listens for mints. It heard one, a thousand years ago, and the sky was soda for a week.
-> Why do you live by the springs?
    Weird Hermit: Someone has to watch them. They bubble in patterns. Three small, one large. Three small, one large.
    Weird Hermit: The village says it is gas. The village does not watch the patterns.
-> What is up the mountain?
    Weird Hermit: Rock candy, and the soda running down through it. At the top, the crater, and the lake, and the corks that float on it.
    Weird Hermit: And the Mint. They left it up there on the rim, where the mountain can see it and be calm. Do not put it back in.
-> Goodbye.
===
